  "The benefit grows even larger when the explanation actually takes place. Teachers often say that they truly understood their subject only after they began to teach it, and research supports this claim. In classrooms where older students tutor younger ones, it is frequently the tutors whose test scores improve the most. {u2|Having to answer an unexpected “why?” from a ten-year-old can be more demanding than any examination.}",
